# Everything in this directory is the cash book itself: bookings, yearly summaries and
# master data (name, address, tax number).
#
# The repository ships three files here on purpose - an empty KABU.DBF, an empty JABU.DBF
# and a STAMM.MEM full of placeholders - so that a clone starts on a clean database and the
# Firststart assistant asks for the identity fields. Once you have filled them in, these
# same paths hold private data, which is why nothing below this line may be committed.
#
# To undo: `git add -f data/<file>` would force it back in. Do not; keep private data out.
*
